{
  "comment": [
    "The UUID qualification's mutation classes.",
    "",
    "Separate from the M16.5 manifest on purpose. That one is 47 classes about",
    "materialized views and migrations and its accounting is closed; mixing these",
    "in would reopen it and make both harder to read. These classes mutate generic",
    "production rules \u2014 the configured-mapping lookup, the capability table, the",
    "eligibility rule, the nullability check \u2014 because that is where uuid actually",
    "lives. Nothing here is a uuid-specific branch invented so that there would be",
    "something to mutate.",
    "",
    "Killers run in the nested module, so they need UUIDCOMPAT_DSN and a database",
    "the qualification has migrated."
  ],
  "evidence_commit": "a196e03",
  "evidence_commit_note": [
    "a196e03 is the revision the mutants were applied to and the killers run at, in",
    "an isolated worktree checked out at exactly that commit. Recording the result",
    "necessarily produces a later commit, because this file is in the repository;",
    "that commit differs from a196e03 by this file alone."
  ],
  "classes": [
    {
      "id": "U01",
      "batch": "U",
      "name": "The configured mapping stops being found by the column's own type name",
      "result": "CAUGHT",
      "mutation": {
        "file": "internal/gen/reconcile/types.go",
        "anchor": "uuidclasses/U01/anchor.txt",
        "replacement": "uuidclasses/U01/replacement.txt",
        "count": 1,
        "expresses": [
          "A column's PostgreSQL type name is no longer one of the keys the configured",
          "mapping is looked up under, so uuid resolves through nothing and a project",
          "whose only statement about the type is types.uuid loses it entirely."
        ]
      },
      "precondition": {
        "expect": [
          "TestUUIDMutationPrecondition/U01"
