      "finding": [
        "Removing the type from writeColumn is not enough to lose it. A column moved",
        "from a domain over uuid to plain uuid \u2014 a schema change with no Go change at",
        "all \u2014 still moves the lock under the mutant, so the fingerprint records the",
        "PostgreSQL type in more than one place.",
        "",
        "That is a property worth having rather than a gap: the fingerprint does not",
        "depend on a single line to notice a type. It does mean the class as stated",
        "cannot be expressed by a one-line mutation, and it is recorded here rather",
        "than left in the manifest as an entry that never runs. The probes written for",
        "it stay in the suite \u2014 they are the only tests that isolate a PostgreSQL-type",
